<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH CROWN SLIPS ON C.BANK GOV COMMENTS - DEALERS.</title>
<headline>CZECH CROWN SLIPS ON C.BANK GOV COMMENTS - DEALERS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech crown slipped on Thursday morning after Czech National Bank (CNB) governor Josef Tosovsky said the recent slowing in M2 money supply growth made room for a possible cut in interest rates.</p>
<p>The crown dropped to +4.32 percent against its mark dollar basket compared with around +4.50 percent before Tosovsky's comments.</p>
</text>
